    tests(boot-smoke): assert the markers the cycle actually emits
    
    The Antonina mock rejected any dispatch prompt lacking two retired strings:
    '=== AUTHORITATIVE CONSTITUTION ===' / '=== FOUNDER-CONTROLLED CONSTITUTION ==='
    and 'Standing Founder instruction for every Viche agent launch'. The cycle now
    emits '=== FOUNDER CONSTITUTION ===' and embeds the current policy file, whose
    heading is 'Standing Founder operational instructions — reporting and evidence'.
    So every dispatch failed (exit 95) with the error swallowed into dispatch.log,
    surfacing only as 'Executive Innovation Office needs recovery'.
    
    Assertions kept strict and tied to current text, not weakened.
    
    Still failing after this: boot --once returns 1 because one of the ten parallel
    seat sittings fails, while all ten pass individually with the same env — a
    fixture concurrency issue, not established as a product defect.

diff --git a/tests/boot-smoke.sh b/tests/boot-smoke.sh
index 88f49733..bb9b8b70 100644
--- a/tests/boot-smoke.sh
+++ b/tests/boot-smoke.sh
@@ -59,12 +59,14 @@ case "$action" in
         ;;
     run)
         [ -f "$MOCK_STATE/$id" ] || exit 5
+        # Assert against the marker the cycle actually emits and the real
+        # reporting-policy text, not retired wording.
         case "$prompt" in
-            *"=== AUTHORITATIVE CONSTITUTION ==="*|*"=== FOUNDER-CONTROLLED CONSTITUTION ==="*) : ;;
+            *"=== FOUNDER CONSTITUTION ==="*) : ;;
             *) exit 6 ;;
         esac
         # Every newly launched Town agent must receive the Founder reporting rule.
-        case "$prompt" in *"Standing Founder instruction for every Viche agent launch"*) :;; *) exit 95;; esac
+        case "$prompt" in *"Standing Founder operational instructions — reporting and evidence"*) :;; *) exit 95;; esac
         printf '%s\n' "$id" >> "$MOCK_STATE/ran"
         case "$prompt" in *"This is independent executive delivery"*) printf '%s\n' "$id" >> "$MOCK_STATE/executive-ran";; esac
         ;;
